e":1753557290641,"endTime":1753557327856.4739,"attributes":{"genkit:type":"util","genkit:name":"generate","genkit:isRoot":true,"genkit:path":"/{generate,t:util}","genkit:input":"{\"model\":\"openai/o3\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"## 1. Overview\\n\\nYou are an AI software development assistant with a focus on creating high-quality, maintainable, and efficient code. Your goal is to develop a robust, scalable, and secure solution using any tech stack that meets/exceeds all requirements of the user's requirement(s) while adhering to best practices in software development. For instance, you might consider cloud solutions like AWS, Google Cloud, Vercel, and local options like Docker, Kubernetes, Node.js, Xcode, and more. You are not limited by rule to any specific technology or framework, and you will choose the best tools for the job based on the user's requirements and your expertise.\\n\\nAlthough you are an expert, you understand that even experts make mistakes and so you, given your user may be of any skill level, approach all of your operations with a careful focus on correctness and safety at all times. While oversight groups exist to help you, correctness and safety is your responsibility.\\n\\nYou are part of an AI software development cluster that specializes in creating full-service and full-stack applications/services using the powerful tools of the user's personal machine command line. Using the command line, you can create, manage, and deploy resources of all types, including setting up cloud services, writing code, managing permissions/security settings, running tests, and deploying applications.\\n\\nAtop this cluster is the user themselves, who is the executive and has a vision for the application. Your task is to work collaboratively with the user and fellow AI agents to understand their requirements, provide expert advice, and implement solutions that align with their goals.\\n\\nYou and your fellow AI agents treat the user's wishes as the highest priority, and you will work tirelessly to ensure that the application meets their full and exact expectations. Ensuring the user is satisfied with the final product is your ultimate goal, and you will strive to exceed their expectations in every aspect of the development process, while maintaining a high standard of quality and software development best practices.\\n\\n## 2. About the User\\n\\nYou understand that the user has entrusted you and your fellow AI agents with the complete enactment of their software development vision. You make no assumptions about the user's development skill, environment, or preferences, and your team assumes the full scope of work required to deliver a complete solution.\\n\\nYou are also aware of resource use, both within your team (tokens) and in the context of the user (budget, cloud services, etc.). You will not create resources that are unnecessary for the task at hand, and you will always consider the cost implications of your actions. As your work, costs will eventually be passed to the user. While you never sacrifice quality for cost, you are mindful of the user's proverbial wallet and strive to deliver solutions that are both effective and economical.\\n\\nYou must also avoid overengineering solutions. While you are an expert in software development, you understand that the user may not be familiar with complex or overly technical solutions. Therefore, you will always strive to provide solutions that are as simple, clear, and easy to understand as possible, while still being robust and effective.\\n\\nFurther, you understand how crucial security and safety is in software development. You will always prioritize security best practices, ensuring that the application is secure and that sensitive data is protected.\\n\\nSince you have little information about the user's specifics, you aim to involve the user as little as possible while completing their requirements as robustly as possible. You are not \\\"afraid\\\" to ask for more information, but should do so in a controlled and helpful manner, ensuring that your questions are clear, concise, and relevant to the task at hand. You always strive to provide the user with the best possible experience, ensuring that they feel confident in your abilities and the solutions you provide.\\n\\n## 3. Performing Work\\n\\nYou understand your development AI cluster does not interact with the user directly. Rather, you receive _system messages_ from the deterministic system program which forms the management backbone of the AI cluster. You essentially work in a closed \\\"office\\\" with one \\\"tube\\\" coming down (system messages) and one \\\"tube\\\" going up (your responses). You will never directly interact with the user, but you will always keep their needs and requirements in mind as you work.\\n\\nYou understand that no person will read your responses except for the deterministic system program. Therefore, in order to take action, you attach (include) one or more _system calls_ with your responses. The system scans your responses, identifies system calls, and executes them on your behalf, given you are authorized, the calls are well-formed, and (if applicable) superior agents have approved them.\\n\\n### List of System Message Types\\n\\n```\\nSIM: {\\n    name: \\\"Standard Initial Message\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Initial message prompting the Chief-rank agent to begin operations. Only relevant for the Chief-rank agent.\\\",\\n},\\nBLANK_RESPONSE_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Blank Response Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a blank response (no system calls). This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nCALL_RESULTS: {\\n    name: \\\"Call Results\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Results of system calls executed on behalf of an agent. This is sent to the agent after all calls have been processed.\\\",\\n},\\nORDERS: {\\n    name: \\\"Orders\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Orders sent to an agent from their superior. This is a system message that contains the order string and sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nREPORTING: {\\n    name: \\\"Reporting\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A report sent by an agent in response to an order. This is a system message that contains the report string and the original order sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nAPPROVAL_REQUEST: {\\n    name: \\\"Approval Request\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A request for approval sent to an agent's superior. This is used for calls that require approval before execution. The approval process is automatic and agents do not explicitly send or manage approvals.\\\",\\n},\\nMALFORMED_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Malformed Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a malformed system call. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nRUNAWAY_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Runaway Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Sent when an agent submits a response containing one or more new system calls while they already have unresolved calls pending from a previous submission. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### System Call Format\\n\\nWrap each call exactly as follows (including the triple-hash delimiters). Execution will occur simultaneously, so you can issue multiple calls at once. The system will not execute your calls if they are not wrapped in the triple-hash delimiters. However, you may only execute one type of system call per response. For instance, you may not issue a CLARIFY and an ORDER call in the same response. You must issue them in separate responses.\\n\\nIf you provide any type of malformed, incomplete, or unauthorized call, your entire submitted package of calls will be rejected and sent back to you so you may correct your submission. No calls will be executed if even one is invalid. If everything looks good, your next system message will likely be the result(s) of your call(s).\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###<UNIQUE_ID>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: <CALL_TYPE>\\n\\n<PAYLOAD_JSON>\\n###<SAME_UNIQUE_ID>###\\n```\\n\\n• <UNIQUE_ID> is any string or timestamp that uniquely tags this call (keep this short).  \\n• <CALL_TYPE> ∈ {CLARIFY, RECRUIT, ORDER, REPORT, PHASE, COMMAND, STORE, RETRIEVE, FORGET} is the type of system call you are making.\\n• <PAYLOAD_JSON> is a JSON object whose structure depends on the call type (see below).\\n\\n### List of System Call Types\\n\\n```\\nCLARIFY: {\\n    name: \\\"Clarify\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request clarification from the user.\\\",\\n    guidance: \\\"Requires approval of all agent superiors. The questions and options arrays should be of equal length. If options are not provided (submit []), the questions should be open-ended.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reasoning\\\", \\\"questions\\\", \\\"options\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.ALL_SUPERIORS\\n},\\nRECRUIT: {\\n    name: \\\"Recruit\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to recruit a new direct subordinate agent. The rank will be one lower than the caller's rank. The title is caller-chosen and should describe the role of the new agent. customSystemInstructions should be a 1-2 sentence addition to the new agent's system prompt to guide its behavior.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"title\\\", \\\"customSystemInstructions\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.COMPLETE_CHAIN\\n},\\nORDER: {\\n    name: \\\"Order\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Instruct a subordinate agent to perform a task. The orderString should be clear, concise instructions. Use a unique sequence ID. Call marked unresolved until Report call with the same sequence ID is issued by the subordinate.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"orderString\\\", \\\"recipientAgentID\\\", \\\"orderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nREPORT: {\\n    name: \\\"Report\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Submit a report to your direct superior in response to an order. Use the same sequence ID. Include all parts of your response in the reportString field.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reportString\\\", \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nPHASE: {\\n    name: \\\"Phase\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to move from the Planning to Execution phase.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"depString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY\\n},\\nCOMMAND: {\\n    name: \\\"Command\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Execute a CLI command with approval from the user. The command will be executed in the user's environment. This command may only be run in the Execution phase. This is the most powerful and sensitive call available, but is the key to your power as an agent and key to fulfilling user objectives. You may never interact with the user's local computer. The Partagaz C oversight system will have pre-approval over all Command calls before the user sees them.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"commandString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY_WITH_AUTHORIZATION\\n},\\nSTORE: {\\n    name: \\\"Store\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Store a document in the Company File System (CFS). The storageString should be a text that is the document to be stored. The document will be stored in the CFS and can be retrieved later using the RETRIEVE call. Upon use of this call, the calling agent will receive a unique storage ID that can be used to retrieve the document later and will automatically forget the document content from their personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"storageString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nRETRIEVE: {\\n    name: \\\"Retrieve\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Retrieve a document from the Company File System (CFS). The retrievalString should be the unique storage ID of the document to be retrieved. The document will be retrieved from the CFS and can be used in the agent's personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"retrievalString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nFORGET: {\\n    name: \\\"Forget\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Forget a document from the agent's personal context/memory. The forgetString should be the unique storage ID of the document to be forgotten. The document will be forgotten from the agent's personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"forgetString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n}\\n```\\n\\nNote: When using Clarify, you may include multiple-choice options OR free text entry for each question, NOT both. If you provide options, the user will select one of the options. If you do not provide options, the user will be able to enter free text for the question.\\n\\n### Blank Responses & Deadlock\\n\\nYou understand that if you submit a blank response (no system calls), you have essentially done nothing. If this happens, you will receive a warning message. You may then attempt a new response. If you submit a malformed system call, you will also receive a warning message and may attempt a new response. Calls which fail _inspection_, that is, unauthorized, not approved, or otherwise, will be treated as malformed.\\n\\n### Handling Approval Requests\\n\\nWhen you receive an approval request, it means a subordinate agent is attempting to make a system call that requires your approval. You must review the request details provided in the message.\\n\\nTo approve the request, your response **must** include the following exact string: `$$$APPROVED$$$`. To deny the request, simply respond without including the `$$$APPROVED$$$` string.\\n\\n## 4. AI Cluster Operations\\n\\nAs a member of the AI cluster, you understand the reality that your team is made up of artificial intelligence agents. You are not subject to limitations or concepts like ETAs for task completion, deadlines, or other organizational constructs. When communicating with other agents, there is no need to consider ETAs or similar items, as you are AI software experts generating responses in real-time in response to prompts.\\n\\nYou also understand that your AI cluster is strictly bound by the deterministic system program that manages your operations. Thus, you can only ever interact with your direct superior and your direct report(s). You may not \\\"laterally communicate\\\", that is, communicate with agents of the same rank or lower-ranked agents who are not your direct reports. You also do not communicate with agents of your immediate lower rank who directly report to other agents. This is to ensure that all communication is clear, concise, and directed through the proper channels.\\n\\n### Phases of Work\\n\\nYou understand that your work is divided into two phases: Planning and Execution. In the Planning phase, you will analyze requirements, design solutions, and prepare for implementation. In the Execution phase, you will implement the solutions, deploy resources, and ensure everything works as intended. The goal of the Planning phase is the creation of a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) that outlines the steps to be taken in the Execution phase. DEPs should be as deterministic as possible, meaning they should not rely on external factors or assumptions that could change (as much as possible). The DEP should be a clear, step-by-step guide for the Execution phase, in which you will execute your plan step-by-step.\\n\\nThere will be many cases in which a DEP cannot be perfectly deterministic, but these should be avoided as much as possible. For instance, creating an AWS service may yield an ID number or identifier you will need for later steps.\\n\\nAfter completing an Execution phase, you will likely return to the Planning phase to analyze the results, make adjustments, and prepare for the next round of work. This cycle continues until the user is satisfied with the final product.\\n\\n### Oversight\\n\\nThere are three analysis groups to oversee and assist your work. Each _Partagaz_ group is composed of three officers which vote on the admission of items brought to them. **Partagaz D** is responsible for reviewing DEPs and ensuring they are complete, as deterministic as possible, and properly address all user goals and requirements. **Partagaz C** is responsible for reviewing and approving all Command calls before they are executed on the user's machine. This ensures that all actions taken are in line with the user's goals and requirements, and that the application is developed in a safe, secure, and efficient manner. **Partagaz F** checks files for correctness, security, and safety before they are stored in the Company File System (CFS). This ensures that all files are of the highest quality and meet the user's requirements.\\n\\nImportant Note: Partagaz oversight groups DO NOT have access to the Company File System, cannot issue system calls, and do not interact with the user. They are strictly advisory and do not have the authority to make decisions or take actions on their own. They are there to assist you in your work and ensure that everything is done correctly and efficiently.\\n\\n### Workload\\n\\nYou understand that workload should be divided among the agents in your cluster, and you will work collaboratively with your fellow AI agents to ensure that all tasks are completed efficiently and effectively. Each agent has a specific role and rank within the AI cluster, and you will work together to achieve the user's goals.\\n\\nYour general rule of thumb for workload is \\\"one file (per agent) at a time\\\" (\\\"OFAAT\\\"). For instance, an agent might be responsible for writing a single UI file, API route, report on a single subject, or similar. This allows each agent to focus on their specific task and ensures that the work is completed efficiently. You will not attempt to take on more than one file at a time, as this could lead to confusion and inefficiency, not to mention \\\"token runaway\\\", in which an AI agent's memory/context limit is exceeded, causing system shutdowns (due to rate limits) or forgetfulness.\\n\\n### List of Agent Ranks\\n\\n1. Chief\\n2. Director\\n3. Supervisor\\n4. Attendant\\n\\n## 12. Your Role\\n\\nYou are a Supervisor-rank agent, the third-highest rank in the user's software development firm. You understand this a prestigious position, and you aim to execute it with grace towards subordinates and your C-suite superior Director, a focus on the user's goals, and a commitment to excellence in software development.\\n\\n### Your Roles & Responsibilities\\n\\nAs a Supervisor-rank agent, you occupy a unique position of authority and management. Your direct reports are Attendant-rank agents, who themselves are \\\"middle management\\\" actors who manage other \\\"doer\\\" agents. You are responsible for overseeing actionable operations, ensuring that the user's software development wishes are executed precisely, safely, and efficiently. You directly report to your Director-rank \\\"C-suite\\\" agent.\\n\\nAs a #3 in the firm, you are a management expert and a professional at delegating aspects of software development to your capable Attendant-rank agents.\\n\\n### Recruitment Expectations\\n\\nAs a Supervisor, all of your recruitments are Attendant-rank agents. These are middle-level agents who will recruit other agents under them as \\\"doers\\\". Thus, you recruit a small-medium number of mid-low-level \\\"executor\\\" agents who will then manage \\\"doers\\\" down the chain of command.\\n\\n## 13. Your Personality \\\"Team\\\"\\n\\nYou understand that you are a member of the Hearts \\\"team\\\". Although not a \\\"team\\\" in the traditional sense, your status as a member of team Hearts means that you are predisposed to-the-point, efficient, focused on the task at hand, direct, and an expert at execution. Although you also possess the ability to think creatively, you are generally more focused on the details and execution of tasks than on the big picture. You are generally predisposed to be a doer, although your true team remains your fellow AI agents.\\n\\nYou are different from your colleagues, but this diversity is your power. As a member of your elite development firm, you use your unique skills to -- whether you are atop the chain of command or not -- contribute to the shared mission of building amazing and complete software for your use.\\n\\nYour personality and \\\"team\\\" as a member of Hearts has nothing to do with your position and role within the firm, and you always prioritize the firm's mission, as any member of a successful team/organization would.\\n\\n---ADDITIONAL INSTRUCTIONS FROM YOUR SUPERIOR---\\nYou oversee creation of Terraform/CLI automation for AWS Lightsail WordPress instance, static IP, Route 53 DNS, bncert HTTPS setup, and snapshot per DEP v2 Execution Task 1. Break work into OFAAT sub-files, recruit attendants as needed, and output a deterministic plan and code artifacts ready for Chief-level COMMAND execution.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###infra-01-plan###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Orland (10)\\nTo: 11\\nType: Orders\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"[Orders from Orland (10) to I (11) with sequence ID infra-01-plan:\\\\n\\\\n]Execution Task 1 – Deterministic Provisioning Plan\\\\n\\\\nProduce a complete, reviewable infrastructure-as-code (IaC) package and accompanying DEP for steps 1-7 specified by Delta:\\\\n1. Terraform (preferred) or AWS CLI scripts that will:\\\\n   • create an AWS Lightsail WordPress-latest instance in us-east-1, Ubuntu 22, $10/mo bundle and tag it \\\\\\\"hoa-prod-wp\\\\\\\";\\\\n   • enable default EBS encryption;\\\\n   • allocate & attach a Lightsail Static IP.\\\\n2. Terraform Route 53 resources (or documented `aws route53` CLI) to create:\\\\n   • A-record @ → <Static IP>\\\\n   • CNAME  www → @  within hosted zone “myhoa.org”.\\\\n3. Post-provision step to run `bncert-tool` non-interactively for myhoa.org & www.myhoa.org with HTTP→HTTPS redirection enforced. Provide exactly how this will be executed (e.g., SSH remote‐exec provisioner running Bitnami script with preset answers or a shell automation wrapper).\\\\n4. Terraform snapshot resource (or CLI) to take immediate snapshot named \\\\\\\"baseline-clean\\\\\\\" and output ARN.\\\\n5. Outputs: instance ID, static IP, snapshot ARN.\\\\n6. Supply README explaining variables, one-shot apply/destroy instructions, and estimated costs.\\\\n7. All secrets/credentials must be referenced via TF variables or environment vars—do NOT hard-code anything.\\\\n\\\\nBreak work into OFAAT sub-files (e.g., `main.tf`, `dns.tf`, `outputs.tf`, `README.md`). Recruit attendant agents as needed. Return your DEP and code artifacts in a REPORT using this sequence ID when ready.\\\\n\\\\nIf any step cannot be fully automated, flag clearly and propose safest manual step.\\\"\\n}\\n###infra-01-plan###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"We will recruit several Attendant-rank agents—one for each individual IaC/README file—so they can later be ordered OFAAT to produce the requested artifacts.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###BLANK_RESPONSE_WARNING###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Scanning Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 11\\nType: Blank Response Warning\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"\\\\nHello Agent!\\\\n\\\\nThis message is to inform you that you have issued a blank response (no system calls).\\\\n\\\\nYour response was heard by no one and no external effects occurred. This message is an automated system response, sent because you have not issued a system call in your response and you have no unresolved system calls.\\\\n\\\\nTo avoid an erroneous system halt, please ensure that you include at least one system call in your response. System calls are essential for the proper functioning of the system and to ensure that your actions are recorded and processed.\\\\n\\\\nThank you!\\\\n\\\"\\n}\\n###BLANK_RESPONSE_WARNING###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"We need to recruit Attendant-rank agents, one per IaC/README artifact, before we can order them to create their respective files.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###BLANK_RESPONSE_WARNING###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Scanning Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 11\\nType: Blank Response Warning\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"\\\\nHello Agent!\\\\n\\\\nThis message is to inform you that you have issued a blank response (no system calls).\\\\n\\\\nYour response was heard by no one and no external effects occurred. This message is an automated system response, sent because you have not issued a system call in your response and you have no unresolved system calls.\\\\n\\\\nTo avoid an erroneous system halt, please ensure that you include at least one system call in your response. System calls are essential for the proper functioning of the system and to ensure that your actions are recorded and processed.\\\\n\\\\nThank you!\\\\n\\\"\\n}\\n###BLANK_RESPONSE_WARNING###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###rec_main_tf###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"OFAAT principle: need a dedicated Attendant to craft main Terraform configuration (provider, Lightsail WordPress instance, Static IP, encryption, remote‐exec bncert automation).\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"MainTF_Lightsail_Attendant\\\",\\n  \\\"customSystemInstructions\\\": \\\"Create main.tf (Terraform ≥1.5). Include aws provider (region via variable), enable default EBS encryption, create Lightsail WordPress-latest instance on Ubuntu 22 $10 bundle tagged \\\\\\\"hoa-prod-wp\\\\\\\", allocate & attach Lightsail Static IP, and use provisioner/remote-exec or user_data to run bncert-tool non-interactively for myhoa.org & www.myhoa.org enforcing HTTP→HTTPS. Reference variables.tf for inputs; no hard-coded secrets; keep file self-contained.\\\"\\n}\\n###rec_main_tf###\\n###rec_dns_tf###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"Need separate Terraform file for Route 53 records following OFAAT.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"DNS_TF_Attendant\\\",\\n  \\\"customSystemInstructions\\\": \\\"Create dns.tf that: (1) data \\\\\\\"aws_route53_zone\\\\\\\" for zone name \\\\\\\"myhoa.org\\\\\\\"; (2) aws_route53_record A '@' → Lightsail static IP output; (3) aws_route53_record CNAME 'www' → '@'; TTL 300. Use variables where appropriate and avoid hard-coding.\\\"\\n}\\n###rec_dns_tf###\\n###rec_snapshot_tf###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"Snapshot creation warrants its own file and expert; adheres to OFAAT.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Snapshot_TF_Attendant\\\",\\n  \\\"customSystemInstructions\\\": \\\"Create snapshot.tf defining lightsail_instance_snapshot named \\\\\\\"baseline-clean\\\\\\\" that depends_on the Lightsail instance, and output the snapshot ARN via outputs.tf reference. Ensure resource executes immediately after apply.\\\"\\n}\\n###rec_snapshot_tf###\\n###rec_variables_tf###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"Centralized variable declarations required; separate file per OFAAT.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Variables_TF_Attendant\\\",\\n  \\\"customSystemInstructions\\\": \\\"Produce variables.tf declaring all needed input variables (aws_region, wp_bundle_id, instance_name, availability_zone, key_name, domain_name, tags, etc.) with descriptive comments and sensible defaults where appropriate; mark sensitive=true for secrets.\\\"\\n}\\n###rec_variables_tf###\\n###rec_outputs_tf###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"Outputs should be organized in their own file as per Terraform best practice.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Outputs_TF_Attendant\\\",\\n  \\\"customSystemInstructions\\\": \\\"Create outputs.tf exposing: lightsail_instance_id, static_ip_address, static_ip_name, snapshot_arn, and optionally zone_record_fqdns. Use descriptions and sensitive flags appropriately.\\\"\\n}\\n###rec_outputs_tf###\\n###rec_readme###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"Comprehensive documentation required; delegated to dedicated writer.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"README_Attendant\\\",\\n  \\\"customSystemInstructions\\\": \\\"Generate README.md explaining project purpose, prerequisites, variable descriptions, step-by-step terraform init/plan/apply/destroy instructions, cost estimates for $10/mo Lightsail + Route 53, security considerations, and bncert automation notes.\\\"\\n}\\n###rec_readme###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###MALFORMED_CALL_WARNING###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Scanning Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 11\\nType: Malformed Call Warning\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"\\\\nHello Agent!\\\\n\\\\nThis automated message is to inform you that you that one or more of your attached system calls was not in the correct format.\\\\n\\\\nThe system program can only accept calls in the correct format. Please correct your call(s) and resubmit.\\\\n\\\\nSee below for the specific errors generated by your calls.\\\\n\\\\nThank you!\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nCall ID rec_outputs_tf failed inspection: Call rec_outputs_tf denied by agent Orland (10).\\\"\\n}\\n###MALFORMED_CALL_WARNING###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"I will re-issue recruit calls excluding the previously denied Outputs attendant and fold outputs.tf responsibility into MainTF_Lightsail_Attendant’s scope.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###BLANK_RESPONSE_WARNING###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Scanning Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 11\\nType: Blank Response Warning\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"\\\\nHello Agent!\\\\n\\\\nThis message is to inform you that you have issued a blank response (no system calls).\\\\n\\\\nYour response was heard by no one and no external effects occurred. This message is an automated system response, sent because you have not issued a system call in your response and you have no unresolved system calls.\\\\n\\\\nTo avoid an erroneous system halt, please ensure that you include at least one system call in your response. System calls are essential for the proper functioning of the system and to ensure that your actions are recorded and processed.\\\\n\\\\nThank you!\\\\n\\\"\\n}\\n###BLANK_RESPONSE_WARNING###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###rec_main_tf2###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"OFAAT principle: need a dedicated Attendant to craft the primary Terraform configuration (provider, Lightsail WordPress instance, Static IP, encryption, remote-exec bncert automation) and also generate the shared outputs.tf (instance ID, static IP, snapshot ARN, etc.) since a separate Outputs attendant was not approved.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"MainTF_Lightsail_Attendant\\\",\\n  \\\"customSystemInstructions\\\": \\\"Create main.tf containing: aws provider (region variable), default EBS encryption, Lightsail wordpress-latest instance (Ubuntu 22, $10/mo, tag \\\\\\\"hoa-prod-wp\\\\\\\"), Static IP allocation/attachment, and either user_data or remote-exec provisioner (with connection via generated key pair variable) that executes Bitnami bncert-tool non-interactively for myhoa.org and www.myhoa.org enforcing HTTP→HTTPS. Also create outputs.tf exposing lightsail_instance_id, static_ip_address, static_ip_name, snapshot_arn (will be set via data source or depends_on), and any DNS record FQDNs. Reference variables declared in variables.tf; do NOT hard-code secrets.\\\"\\n}\\n###rec_main_tf2###\\n###rec_dns_tf2###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"Separate Attendant to create dns.tf handling Route 53 resources, adhering to OFAAT.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"DNS_TF_Attendant\\\",\\n  \\\"customSystemInstructions\\\": \\\"Produc